data: {"type":"block","block":{"type":"WritingDraft","id":"turn-5583b8013dcc-writing-draft","meta":{"status":"ready","error":null},"data":{"kind":"outline","title":"Outline on Retrieval in Retrieval-Augmented Generation","sections":[{"heading":"Retrieval Fundamentals and Sources","segments":[{"text":"Retrieval in RAG centers on efficiently finding relevant documents from a data source, and it involves choices about the source, granularity, pre-processing and embedding model.","citationIds":["c1"],"speaker":null},{"text":"Sources have broadened from plain text to semi-structured data such as PDFs and structured data such as knowledge graphs. There is also a growing trend of retrieving from content produced by LLMs themselves.","citationIds":["c1"],"speaker":null}]},{"heading":"Retrieval Techniques","segments":[{"text":"Hybrid strategies combine keyword, semantic and vector search to serve varied queries. HyDE aims to improve relevance by comparing embeddings of generated answers with real documents.","citationIds":["c2"],"speaker":null},{"text":"In graph settings, an integrated retriever can pair rule-based symbolic retrieval with embedding-based neural retrieval. This balances precision against adaptability and generalizability.","citationIds":["c3"],"speaker":null}]},{"heading":"Retrieval Processes","segments":[{"text":"Iterative retrieval repeatedly searches the knowledge base using the initial query plus the text generated so far. Multiple rounds give added context and can make later answers more robust.","citationIds":["c4"],"speaker":null},{"text":"Adaptive retrieval lets the system decide on its own whether retrieval is needed and when to stop, as in FLARE and Self-RAG.","citationIds":["c4","c2"],"speaker":null}]},{"heading":"Evaluating Retrieval","segments":[{"text":"Retrieval can be measured with recall@k, precision@k and F1@k, and one study counts a document as retrieved if any of its chunks is retrieved.","citationIds":["c5"],"speaker":null},{"text":"Other work reports recall@2 and recall@5 for retrieval, and compares single-step methods against multi-step ones.","citationIds":["c6"],"speaker":null}]}],"citations":[{"id":"c1","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f22af6d01a52a8fb","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":5,"quote":"it is crucial to efficiently retrieve relevant documents from the data source."},{"id":"c2","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_445a807c7c2b8b50","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":5,"quote":"Hybrid retrieval strategies integrate keyword, semantic, and vector searches to cater to diverse queries."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_9d1c3f70428d0475","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":35,"quote":"Integrating them together provides a better trade-off between rule-based precision and neural-based adaptability and generalizabili"},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_18d9f568d1c19f4e","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":10,"quote":"Iterative retrieval is a process where the knowledge base is repeatedly searched based on the initial query and the text generated so far"},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_26249f4bdc41b629","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":9,"quote":"a document is considered retrieved if any chunk from it is retrieved, irrespective of the query-chunk relevance score."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_1561f63effe8dae8","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":5,"quote":"We report retrieval and QA performance on the datasets above using recall@2 and recall@5 (R@2 and R@5 below) for